          BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION

 IN THE MATTER OF SOUTHWESTERN                                 )
 PUBLIC SERVICE COMPANY’S APPLICATION                          )
 FOR: (1) REVISION OF ITS RETAIL RATES                         ) Docket No. 25-00079-UT
 UNDER ADVICE NOTICE 341; AND (2) OTHER                        )
 ASSOCIATED RELIEF                                             )

                         ORDER SUSPENDING ADVICE NOTICE 341

       THIS MATTER comes before the New Mexico Public Regulation Commission

(“Commission”) upon Southwestern Public Service Company’s (“SPS”) Application for Authority

to Change Rates and for Other Approvals and Authorizations with Schedules A-1 through Q-6 (the

“Application”). Accompanying the Application, SPS filed Advice Notice No. 341, which

incorporates the requests included in the Application.

       The Commission finds that a hearing should be held concerning the reasonableness of the

proposed rates and accordingly suspends the operation of Advice Notice No. 341 for an initial

period of nine-months. 1

                                           BACKGROUND

        1.      On November 20, 2025, SPS filed the Application requesting authority to change

its base rates and certain other approvals. 2 Specifically, SPS requests to increase its base rate

charges for the New Mexico retail jurisdiction by $175,354,544, a 24.25% increase over current

base rate revenue and 16.73% in total revenues, based on a total New Mexico retail revenue

requirements of $892,652,373 for the Future Test Year running from December 1, 2026, through

November 30, 2027. 3 The Application includes a request for an overall weighted average cost of



1 Per Section 62-8-7 of the Public Utility Act, the Commission may extend the suspension period for an

additional three months if the Commission finds that a longer time will be required. NMSA 1978, §62-8-7(C)
(2011).
2 Application at 1.,
3 Id. at 3.
 capital (“WACC”) of 8.21% for the Future Test Year, reflecting a 56% equity ratio, an authorized

return on equity (“ROE”) of 10.5%, and a cost of debt of 5.29%. 4 The Application includes

requests for several other approvals, summarized in the 1600-page filing and in the testimonies of

29 SPS witnesses. 5

          2.    Accompanying the Application is Advice Notice 341 and associated rate

schedules. The proposed rates in Advice Notice No. 341 have an effective date of December 20,

2025. 6

          3.    On November 26, 2025, the Commission issued an order appointing co-hearing

examiners to preside over this matter. 7

                                            DISCUSSION

          4.    When an application proposing new rates is filed with the Commission, the

Commission may hold a hearing concerning the reasonableness of the proposed rates. 8 If the

Commission deems it necessary to assess the reasonableness of a proposed rate, the Commission

shall suspend the operation of the proposed rate before the effective date, for an initial period of

nine months. 9 The Commission may extend the period for an additional three months if deemed

necessary. 10

          5.    Given the breadth of the Application and the implications the Application will have

on New Mexico ratepayers, a hearing is necessary to assess the reasonableness of the proposed

rates. Accordingly, Advice Notice 341 shall be suspended for an initial period of nine months as


