 of the proposed effective date. The Commission may later extend the period of suspension for an

additional three months if the Commission deems such an extension to be necessary.

                               FINDINGS AND CONCLUSIONS

       6.       The Commission finds a hearing is necessary to assess the reasonableness of the

proposed rates, and Advice Notice 341 should be suspended for an initial period of nine months

beyond the effective date of December 20, 2025, to hold said hearing. The Commission may extend

the suspension period for an additional three months if the Commission determines that a longer

time will be required.

       IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

       A.       The proposed rates filed by SPS in Advice Notice No. 341 are suspended for an

initial period of nine months, commencing on December 20, 2025.

       B.       This Order is effective when signed.

       C.       The Commission shall serve a copy of this Order upon all persons listed on the

attached Certificate of Service via e-mail if their e-mail addresses are known, and otherwise, via

regular mail.

       D.       In computing time in accordance with statute, regulation, or Commission order, the

computation shall begin on the date that this Order is filed with the Chief Clerk of the

Commission’s Records Management Bureau or the Chief Clerk’s designee.




